{
    "word": "theodolite",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "299e2ab7-c4b4-33a7-bd3a-2c65158df46f",
                "word": "theodolite",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "884173fe-4dbb-4df0-b235-e4dd669b6d9f",
                        "entry_id": "299e2ab7-c4b4-33a7-bd3a-2c65158df46f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "theodolites"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2c06e0eb-1141-35f5-85fa-96ad3b7187d9",
                        "entry_id": "299e2ab7-c4b4-33a7-bd3a-2c65158df46f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A surveying instrument, consisting of a small mounted telescope, used to measure horizontal and vertical angles."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a73d8a83-5b84-4896-a7e6-662d3b0f88be",
                                "sense_id": "2c06e0eb-1141-35f5-85fa-96ad3b7187d9",
                                "text": "I drew outlines (according to my usual custom) of all the hills on the horizon before us, and took angles on them with the theodolite."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f376cda-cce9-443e-b8cb-5da8fe5054b9",
                                "sense_id": "2c06e0eb-1141-35f5-85fa-96ad3b7187d9",
                                "text": "The height of those mountains was from five to seven thousand feet above our level, by angular measurement with a theodolite."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1617a8fe-d948-4f28-af65-c24776a84a6b",
                                "sense_id": "2c06e0eb-1141-35f5-85fa-96ad3b7187d9",
                                "text": "It was a lieutenant and a couple of privates of the 8th Hussars, with a stand like a theodolite, which the artilleryman told me was a heliograph."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c71d9f54-aceb-49ee-bc16-bfb5e09255e0",
                                "sense_id": "2c06e0eb-1141-35f5-85fa-96ad3b7187d9",
                                "text": "Germany, of all countries, was most vitally concerned in it; but even a cave-dweller in La Fayette Square, seeking only a measure of motion since the Crusades, saw before his eyes, in the spring of 1903, a survey of future order or anarchy that would exhaust the power of his telescopes and defy the accuracy of his theodolites."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dbbf4bf8-ee8b-4ced-9647-0c411486e60d",
                                "sense_id": "2c06e0eb-1141-35f5-85fa-96ad3b7187d9",
                                "text": "The process of setting up a theodolite is carried out in three stages: centring the theodolite, levelling the theodolite and elimination of parallax."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
